Feature: progress-indicator-fixes (RETROACTIVE — commit d489425, logged after the
changelog/ convention was introduced in 478c817)
Target module: ProgressIndicator

- The constructor's default progress space was never usable: getProgressSpaceElement
  returned undefined whenever defaultProgressSpace was set; resolution order is now
  progressSpaceId attribute -> passed element -> default space, and the constructor
  argument is validated.
- showProgress/hideProgress callable without an element when a default space exists,
  with a clear error otherwise.
- hideProgress clears the actual crawl interval (smallIncrement) instead of the
  no-op clearInterval(tinyIncrement), which leaked the timer on slow requests.
- Re-showing a finished style 3 bar resets it to 0% instead of animating backwards
  from 100%.

Affected projects: any consumer of vUX-progressIndicator.js, notably the SPA example
which relies on the default-space constructor form.
